{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>משנאי יכחשו</b> — like <i>your enemies will deny you</i>: out of the abundance of their terror they will deny having rebelled against you. Or after the manner of <i>and your enemies will deny you</i>, for the reason that <i>my flesh wasted away from fat</i>. [n: Ibn Ezra compares usages where the root כחש conveys wasting/shrinking alongside denying; the second parallel cited is Deut. 32:37, the third Psalms 109:24.]" "<b>והיה עתם</b> — for his day comes and they will never rise. R. Judah ben Balaam said: likewise <i>I will turn my hand against their foes</i> — for they are the enemies of YHWH, for they deny His divinity, and they reckoned that they would stand forever; and this is a far-fetched interpretation and it is not according to the rules of the sacred tongue — <i>Is it not, and it is near to come?</i> And many are like this. [n: Ibn Ezra rebuts R. Judah ben Balaam's reading, which apparently links משנאי and יכחשו to neighboring verses; the phrase <i>הלא ראה וקרוב לבא עתה</i> echoes Malachi 3:1 or a comparable idiom, affirming the plain sense is imminent, not allegorical.]"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 81, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:51.141461553Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}